{
  "name": "bad-data-body",
  "integration": "runzero-task-sync",
  "script": "runzero-task-sync/runzero-task-sync.star",
  "description": "A task whose data download answers 200 with a body that is neither JSON nor gzip -- an HTML proxy page is the realistic shape. The old first-byte sniff fed anything not starting with '{' straight to gzip_decompress, which raises on such a body and aborts the whole run, silently skipping every later task. The guard must skip THAT task with a log line and carry on: the healthy task after it is still downloaded, imported, and hidden. The healthy task's hide then answers 500, which must also be logged rather than silent -- with hide_tasks_on_sync on, a persistently failing hide re-syncs the same task every run with no visible cause. The failed-body task must never be hidden and never be imported.",
